t practice (scope_4) and any separate current/voltage lesson so that the actual teacher-written items can be solved, explained and checked. This keeps the work bounded and focused on the real assessment rather than on invented practice.","unreviewedPhaseRefs":[],"splits":[{"planRef":"plan_1","originalRef":"quiz_work","pieceRefs":["quiz_work_part_1","quiz_work_part_2"],"originalActivity":{"localId":"quiz_work","outcomeRefs":["phase_quiz"],"scopeRefs":["scope_1","scope_2","scope_3"],"title":"Work, explain and check the actual teacher quiz items","activityType":"Assignment completion with explanation and error correction","purpose":"To solve the real quiz items, state the current/voltage and series/parallel reasoning behind each answer, and correct actual errors before the quiz.","instructions":"Obtain the actual teacher-written quiz (or the exact items your teacher provided). Work through each item in order. For every item: (1) write the given values and what is asked; (2) state which rule you are using and why it applies (for example, in a series branch the current is the same through each component, so voltages add; in parallel branches the voltage is the same across each branch, so currents add); (3) solve showing your steps; (4) check your answer against the item's own data (for example, confirm the branch currents sum to the total current, or the component voltages sum to the source voltage). If an item involves a combination of series and parallel parts, split it into those parts and apply the same rules. When you find an error, mark it, explain what rule you misapplied, and re-solve that item correctly. If you cannot obtain the actual items, tell me and we will use only the items the teacher has given you — do not substitute invented questions. Do not spend time on mixed-circuit practice beyond what the actual items require.","completionCriterion":"Every actual quiz item has a written solution, a stated rule and reason, a check, and any error found is corrected