activities.instructions:
Without copying first_program.py, write a new file independent_program.py that:
- stores at least one text value and two numeric values in clearly named variables;
- computes one new numeric value from them;
- prints a formatted f-string summary line;
- uses if/else (and optionally elif) to print a different message for at least two different value ranges.
Choose your own theme, e.g. a budget check, a score band, or a shipping cost estimate. Run it, fix any errors yourself, and run it with at least two different sets of values so both branches are exercised. Add a short comment block explaining the rule your program implements.
If you get stuck on a specific error, write down the exact message and what you tried; do not paste in a solution from elsewhere.

